-- title:
--   Reduced special fibre of the j-chart ring of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M$ with $M \neq 0$, $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L((q))$ over $L$, assumed equal to the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise ring map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$, i.e. of the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ attached to $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with an algebra structure over which $L$ is its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$; let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be an element whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of the rational Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the $j$-numerator power series, and assume $j \neq 0$. Write $\mathcal{O}$ for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of all elements integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j$. Then the quotient of $\mathcal{O}$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ under $A \to \mathcal{O}$ is a reduced ring.
--
--   This is the statement that the special fibre of the $j$-finite affine chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ is reduced; note that the fibre is taken over the residue field of $A$, i.e. modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A = (1-\zeta_p)$ in the intended case $A = \mathbb{Z}_p[\zeta_p]$, and not modulo $p$. It feeds the construction of a finite étale quotient of the chart ring cut out by a polynomial condition on $j$, used in the analysis of the reduction of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$.
